{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SQmhWpZ5VtuwFvAtqjEKkn","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Audiobook Prep Output Quality Rubric\n     2→\n     3→This rubric defines evaluation criteria for audiobook narrator preparation documents. Use this to assess analysis output quality.\n     4→\n     5→## Scoring Overview\n     6→\n     7→| Category | Weight | Focus |\n     8→|----------|--------|-------|\n     9→| Structure Detection | 20% | Chapter boundaries, front/back matter |\n    10→| Character Extraction | 25% | All characters identified, correct aliases |\n    11→| Character Profiles | 15% | Accurate descriptions, relationships |\n    12→| Chapter Summaries | 20% | Key events, narrator-useful details |\n    13→| Pronunciation Guide | 10% | Unusual words flagged, no false positives |\n    14→| HTML Presentation | 10% | Navigation, readability, organization |\n    15→\n    16→**Threshold:** Overall score >= 8.0 to pass\n    17→\n    18→---\n    19→\n    20→## Category Details\n    21→\n    22→### 1. Structure Detection (Weight: 20%)\n    23→\n    24→**What we're measuring:** Did the tool correctly identify the book's organization?\n    25→\n    26→| Score | Criteria |\n    27→|-------|----------|\n    28→| 10 | Perfect: All chapters identified, correct boundaries, handles unusual structures |\n    29→| 8-9 | Excellent: All major divisions correct, minor issues with epigraphs or breaks |\n    30→| 6-7 | Good: Most chapters correct, some boundary errors or missed subdivisions |\n    31→| 4-5 | Fair: Significant errors but majority of structure captured |\n    32→| 1-3 | Poor: Major structural errors, merged or missing chapters |\n    33→| 0 | Failed: Structure completely wrong or not detected |\n    34→\n    35→**Checklist:**\n    36→- [ ] All chapters detected (compare to expected chapter count)\n    37→- [ ] Chapter titles extracted correctly\n    38→- [ ] Front matter (dedication, preface) identified separately\n    39→- [ ] Back matter (notes, appendices) identified separately\n    40→- [ ] No merged chapters (two chapters treated as one)\n    41→- [ ] No split chapters (one chapter treated as multiple)\n    42→- [ ] Roman numerals handled correctly\n    43→- [ ] \"Chapter\" vs \"Book\" vs \"Part\" hierarchy correct\n    44→\n    45→---\n    46→\n    47→### 2. Character Extraction (Weight: 25%)\n    48→\n    49→**What we're measuring:** Are all significant characters identified with correct information?\n    50→\n    51→| Score | Criteria |\n    52→|-------|----------|\n    53→| 10 | Perfect: All named characters, correct aliases, accurate relationships |\n    54→| 8-9 | Excellent: All major characters, most minor, few alias issues |\n    55→| 6-7 | Good: Major characters correct, some missing minors or alias errors |\n    56→| 4-5 | Fair: Main characters present but significant gaps or errors |\n    57→| 1-3 | Poor: Major characters missing or incorrectly merged/split |\n    58→| 0 | Failed: Character extraction completely wrong |\n    59→\n    60→**Checklist:**\n    61→- [ ] All major characters (>10 mentions) identified\n    62→- [ ] No false character splits (same person as two entries)\n    63→- [ ] No false character merges (two people as one entry)\n    64→- [ ] Aliases correctly grouped (full name = nickname = title+name)\n    65→- [ ] Titles handled correctly (Dr., Mr., Mrs., etc.)\n    66→- [ ] Nicknames linked to canonical names\n    67→- [ ] No hallucinated characters (entries that don't exist in text)\n    68→- [ ] First appearance chapter is accurate\n    69→\n    70→**Common Issues:**\n    71→- Characters sharing surnames incorrectly merged (spouses, siblings)\n    72→- Full names and nicknames not linked\n    73→- Titled references (Mr. X) not linked to full names\n    74→- Minor characters filtered out too aggressively\n    75→\n    76→---\n    77→\n    78→### 3. Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\n    79→\n    80→**What we're measuring:** Are character descriptions accurate and useful for narration?\n    81→\n    82→| Score | Criteria |\n    83→|-------|----------|\n    84→| 10 | Perfect: Rich, accurate descriptions with voice notes and relationships |\n    85→| 8-9 | Excellent: Good descriptions, accurate relationships, useful details |\n    86→| 6-7 | Good: Basic descriptions correct, some missing depth |\n    87→| 4-5 | Fair: Descriptions present but thin or partially inaccurate |\n    88→| 1-3 | Poor: Descriptions wrong or mostly missing |\n    89→| 0 | Failed: No useful profile information |\n    90→\n    91→**Checklist:**\n    92→- [ ] Physical descriptions match text (when provided)\n    93→- [ ] Personality traits supported by text evidence\n    94→- [ ] Key relationships identified (family, romantic, professional)\n    95→- [ ] No invented details (information not in the source text)\n    96→- [ ] Speech patterns or dialect noted (when present)\n    97→- [ ] Character arc summary useful for narrator\n    98→\n    99→---\n   100→\n   101→### 4. Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\n   102→\n   103→**What we're measuring:** Do summaries help a narrator prepare for each chapter?\n   104→\n   105→| Score | Criteria |\n   106→|-------|----------|\n   107→| 10 | Perfect: Accurate, comprehensive, narrator-focused summaries |\n   108→| 8-9 | Excellent: Captures key events and tone, useful for prep |\n   109→| 6-7 | Good: Main events correct, some gaps or minor errors |\n   110→| 4-5 | Fair: Partially accurate but missing key events or has errors |\n   111→| 1-3 | Poor: Major inaccuracies or missing most content |\n   112→| 0 | Failed: Summaries wrong or not generated |\n   113→\n   114→**Checklist:**\n   115→- [ ] Key plot events captured (3-5 per chapter minimum)\n   116→- [ ] Characters appearing in chapter mentioned\n   117→- [ ] No hallucinated events (things that didn't happen)\n   118→- [ ] No major spoilers from future chapters\n   119→- [ ] Tone and mood indicated (useful for narrator)\n   120→- [ ] Length appropriate (100-300 words)\n   121→- [ ] Setting/location changes noted\n   122→\n   123→---\n   124→\n   125→### 5. Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\n   126→\n   127→**What we're measuring:** Are unusual words flagged with helpful pronunciation info?\n   128→\n   129→| Score | Criteria |\n   130→|-------|----------|\n   131→| 10 | Perfect: All unusual words flagged, accurate IPA, no false positives |\n   132→| 8-9 | Excellent: Good coverage, mostly accurate, few false positives |\n   133→| 6-7 | Good: Most unusual words caught, some gaps or errors |\n   134→| 4-5 | Fair: Partial coverage, noticeable gaps or many false positives |\n   135→| 1-3 | Poor: Major gaps or mostly incorrect |\n   136→| 0 | Failed: No useful pronunciation information |\n   137→\n   138→**Checklist:**\n   139→- [ ] Foreign words/phrases identified\n   140→- [ ] Unusual proper nouns flagged (names, places)\n   141→- [ ] Period-specific terms noted\n   142→- [ ] IPA provided and accurate (when present)\n   143→- [ ] No common words flagged (false positives)\n   144→- [ ] Context provided for homographs (read vs. read, lead vs. lead)\n   145→- [ ] Regional/dialect pronunciations noted\n   146→\n   147→---\n   148→\n   149→### 6. HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\n   150→\n   151→**What we're measuring:** Is the output professional and usable?\n   152→\n   153→| Score | Criteria |\n   154→|-------|----------|\n   155→| 10 | Perfect: Clean, navigable, print-ready, professional appearance |\n   156→| 8-9 | Excellent: Well-organized, easy to use, minor polish issues |\n   157→| 6-7 | Good: Functional and readable, some UX improvements possible |\n   158→| 4-5 | Fair: Usable but awkward navigation or formatting issues |\n   159→| 1-3 | Poor: Difficult to use, significant formatting problems |\n   160→| 0 | Failed: Broken or unreadable |\n   161→\n   162→**Checklist:**\n   163→- [ ] Navigation works (can jump to chapters, characters)\n   164→- [ ] Typography is readable\n   165→- [ ] Information is logically organized\n   166→- [ ] No broken elements or missing sections\n   167→- [ ] Prints cleanly (if applicable)\n   168→\n   169→---\n   170→\n   171→## Scoring Formula\n   172→\n   173→```\n   174→Overall = (\n   175→    Structure × 0.20 +\n   176→    Characters × 0.25 +\n   177→    Profiles × 0.15 +\n   178→    Summaries × 0.20 +\n   179→    Pronunciation × 0.10 +\n   180→    Presentation × 0.10\n   181→)\n   182→```\n   183→\n   184→**Thresholds:**\n   185→- **>= 8.0**: PASS - advance to next text\n   186→- **< 8.0**: FAIL - iterate with fixes\n   187→\n   188→---\n   189→\n   190→## Issue Severity Classification\n   191→\n   192→When scoring below threshold, classify issues for the fix phase:\n   193→\n   194→### CRITICAL (blocks progress, score impact > 1 point)\n   195→- Character merge/split errors for main characters\n   196→- Missing major characters\n   197→- Completely wrong chapter structure\n   198→- Hallucinated content\n   199→\n   200→### HIGH (significant impact, score impact 0.5-1 point)\n   201→- Missing minor but named characters\n   202→- Incorrect relationships for main characters\n   203→- Multiple chapter summary errors\n   204→- Major pronunciation gaps\n   205→\n   206→### MEDIUM (noticeable but manageable, score impact < 0.5)\n   207→- Minor character description inaccuracies\n   208→- Excessive false positives in pronunciation\n   209→- Formatting/presentation issues\n   210→- Missing some aliases\n   211→\n   212→### LOW (polish items)\n   213→- Minor wording improvements\n   214→- Edge case handling\n   215→- Performance optimizations\n   216→\n   217→---\n   218→\n   219→## Evaluation Notes\n   220→\n   221→### Use Your Knowledge\n   222→The evaluator (Claude) has literary knowledge of classic texts. Use this knowledge to:\n   223→- Verify character completeness against known casts\n   224→- Check summary accuracy against known plots\n   225→- Validate relationships and aliases\n   226→\n   227→### Be Specific\n   228→Instead of: \"Character extraction has issues\"\n   229→Write: \"Jay Gatsby and 'Gatsby' are listed as separate characters. These should be merged as aliases.\"\n   230→\n   231→### Be Actionable\n   232→Include file locations and suggested fixes when possible:\n   233→- \"Likely cause: alias resolution in src/agents/characters.py\"\n   234→- \"Suggested fix: improve fuzzy matching for FirstName-LastName to LastName\"\n   235→\n   236→### Focus on Threshold\n   237→If score is 7.8, focus only on what's needed to cross 8.0. Don't enumerate every possible improvement.\n   238→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f12b5706-a002-4f0f-88f7-e989353376ac","uuid":"1efc5b4b-839a-4557-9f74-2fab31960447","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/spec/output_quality.md","content":"# Audiobook Prep Output Quality Rubric\n\nThis rubric defines evaluation criteria for audiobook narrator preparation documents. Use this to assess analysis output quality.\n\n## Scoring Overview\n\n| Category | Weight | Focus |\n|----------|--------|-------|\n| Structure Detection | 20% | Chapter boundaries, front/back matter |\n| Character Extraction | 25% | All characters identified, correct aliases |\n| Character Profiles | 15% | Accurate descriptions, relationships |\n| Chapter Summaries | 20% | Key events, narrator-useful details |\n| Pronunciation Guide | 10% | Unusual words flagged, no false positives |\n| HTML Presentation | 10% | Navigation, readability, organization |\n\n**Threshold:** Overall score >= 8.0 to pass\n\n---\n\n## Category Details\n\n### 1. Structure Detection (Weight: 20%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Did the tool correctly identify the book's organization?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: All chapters identified, correct boundaries, handles unusual structures |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: All major divisions correct, minor issues with epigraphs or breaks |\n| 6-7 | Good: Most chapters correct, some boundary errors or missed subdivisions |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Significant errors but majority of structure captured |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major structural errors, merged or missing chapters |\n| 0 | Failed: Structure completely wrong or not detected |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] All chapters detected (compare to expected chapter count)\n- [ ] Chapter titles extracted correctly\n- [ ] Front matter (dedication, preface) identified separately\n- [ ] Back matter (notes, appendices) identified separately\n- [ ] No merged chapters (two chapters treated as one)\n- [ ] No split chapters (one chapter treated as multiple)\n- [ ] Roman numerals handled correctly\n- [ ] \"Chapter\" vs \"Book\" vs \"Part\" hierarchy correct\n\n---\n\n### 2. Character Extraction (Weight: 25%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Are all significant characters identified with correct information?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: All named characters, correct aliases, accurate relationships |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: All major characters, most minor, few alias issues |\n| 6-7 | Good: Major characters correct, some missing minors or alias errors |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Main characters present but significant gaps or errors |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major characters missing or incorrectly merged/split |\n| 0 | Failed: Character extraction completely wrong |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] All major characters (>10 mentions) identified\n- [ ] No false character splits (same person as two entries)\n- [ ] No false character merges (two people as one entry)\n- [ ] Aliases correctly grouped (full name = nickname = title+name)\n- [ ] Titles handled correctly (Dr., Mr., Mrs., etc.)\n- [ ] Nicknames linked to canonical names\n- [ ] No hallucinated characters (entries that don't exist in text)\n- [ ] First appearance chapter is accurate\n\n**Common Issues:**\n- Characters sharing surnames incorrectly merged (spouses, siblings)\n- Full names and nicknames not linked\n- Titled references (Mr. X) not linked to full names\n- Minor characters filtered out too aggressively\n\n---\n\n### 3. Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Are character descriptions accurate and useful for narration?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: Rich, accurate descriptions with voice notes and relationships |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Good descriptions, accurate relationships, useful details |\n| 6-7 | Good: Basic descriptions correct, some missing depth |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Descriptions present but thin or partially inaccurate |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Descriptions wrong or mostly missing |\n| 0 | Failed: No useful profile information |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] Physical descriptions match text (when provided)\n- [ ] Personality traits supported by text evidence\n- [ ] Key relationships identified (family, romantic, professional)\n- [ ] No invented details (information not in the source text)\n- [ ] Speech patterns or dialect noted (when present)\n- [ ] Character arc summary useful for narrator\n\n---\n\n### 4. Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Do summaries help a narrator prepare for each chapter?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: Accurate, comprehensive, narrator-focused summaries |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Captures key events and tone, useful for prep |\n| 6-7 | Good: Main events correct, some gaps or minor errors |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Partially accurate but missing key events or has errors |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major inaccuracies or missing most content |\n| 0 | Failed: Summaries wrong or not generated |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] Key plot events captured (3-5 per chapter minimum)\n- [ ] Characters appearing in chapter mentioned\n- [ ] No hallucinated events (things that didn't happen)\n- [ ] No major spoilers from future chapters\n- [ ] Tone and mood indicated (useful for narrator)\n- [ ] Length appropriate (100-300 words)\n- [ ] Setting/location changes noted\n\n---\n\n### 5. Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Are unusual words flagged with helpful pronunciation info?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: All unusual words flagged, accurate IPA, no false positives |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Good coverage, mostly accurate, few false positives |\n| 6-7 | Good: Most unusual words caught, some gaps or errors |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Partial coverage, noticeable gaps or many false positives |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major gaps or mostly incorrect |\n| 0 | Failed: No useful pronunciation information |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] Foreign words/phrases identified\n- [ ] Unusual proper nouns flagged (names, places)\n- [ ] Period-specific terms noted\n- [ ] IPA provided and accurate (when present)\n- [ ] No common words flagged (false positives)\n- [ ] Context provided for homographs (read vs. read, lead vs. lead)\n- [ ] Regional/dialect pronunciations noted\n\n---\n\n### 6. HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\n\n**What we're measuring:** Is the output professional and usable?\n\n| Score | Criteria |\n|-------|----------|\n| 10 | Perfect: Clean, navigable, print-ready, professional appearance |\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Well-organized, easy to use, minor polish issues |\n| 6-7 | Good: Functional and readable, some UX improvements possible |\n| 4-5 | Fair: Usable but awkward navigation or formatting issues |\n| 1-3 | Poor: Difficult to use, significant formatting problems |\n| 0 | Failed: Broken or unreadable |\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] Navigation works (can jump to chapters, characters)\n- [ ] Typography is readable\n- [ ] Information is logically organized\n- [ ] No broken elements or missing sections\n- [ ] Prints cleanly (if applicable)\n\n---\n\n## Scoring Formula\n\n```\nOverall = (\n    Structure × 0.20 +\n    Characters × 0.25 +\n    Profiles × 0.15 +\n    Summaries × 0.20 +\n    Pronunciation × 0.10 +\n    Presentation × 0.10\n)\n```\n\n**Thresholds:**\n- **>= 8.0**: PASS - advance to next text\n- **< 8.0**: FAIL - iterate with fixes\n\n---\n\n## Issue Severity Classification\n\nWhen scoring below threshold, classify issues for the fix phase:\n\n### CRITICAL (blocks progress, score impact > 1 point)\n- Character merge/split errors for main characters\n- Missing major characters\n- Completely wrong chapter structure\n- Hallucinated content\n\n### HIGH (significant impact, score impact 0.5-1 point)\n- Missing minor but named characters\n- Incorrect relationships for main characters\n- Multiple chapter summary errors\n- Major pronunciation gaps\n\n### MEDIUM (noticeable but manageable, score impact < 0.5)\n- Minor character description inaccuracies\n- Excessive false positives in pronunciation\n- Formatting/presentation issues\n- Missing some aliases\n\n### LOW (polish items)\n- Minor wording improvements\n- Edge case handling\n- Performance optimizations\n\n---\n\n## Evaluation Notes\n\n### Use Your Knowledge\nThe evaluator (Claude) has literary knowledge of classic texts. Use this knowledge to:\n- Verify character completeness against known casts\n- Check summary accuracy against known plots\n- Validate relationships and aliases\n\n### Be Specific\nInstead of: \"Character extraction has issues\"\nWrite: \"Jay Gatsby and 'Gatsby' are listed as separate characters. These should be merged as aliases.\"\n\n### Be Actionable\nInclude file locations and suggested fixes when possible:\n- \"Likely cause: alias resolution in src/agents/characters.py\"\n- \"Suggested fix: improve fuzzy matching for FirstName-LastName to LastName\"\n\n### Focus on Threshold\nIf score is 7.8, focus only on what's needed to cross 8.0. Don't enumerate every possible improvement.\n","numLines":238,"startLine":1,"totalLines":238}}}
